      {"@type":"Question","name":"What is TDI scanning?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"TDI (Time Delay Integration) is a scanning technique that accumulates signal across multiple detector rows as an object moves through the X-ray beam — delivering high sensitivity at high conveyor speeds."}},
